+\documentclass[11pt,oneside]{memoir}
+\usepackage{raeez-math-template}
+\title{Translated ordered states and native Heisenberg collisions}
+\author{}
+\date{}
+\begin{document}
+\maketitle
+\begin{abstract}
+Differentiating the ordered multiplication kernel determines the products of translated states.
+These products define a flat differential module and retain the original ordered bar as its untranslated subcomplex.
+At a fixed nonzero Heisenberg level, weighted edge integrals give binary and ternary graded comparisons with the native chiral complex.
+Their defects determine minimal added collision modules for these prescribed maps.
+The ternary addition contains three pair-diagonal modules and a current module on the small diagonal.
+Exact sequences describe its cohomology relative to the original ordered source.
+A four-current calculation determines the next differential, supported on the three double-pair diagonals.
+\end{abstract}
